DESCRIPTION:The Appalachian Mountaineer is a cousin the Journey\, in that i
 t is also in Virginia\, run on gravel\, and built with the same stoke and 
 fire you expect in Floyd in the spring. But that’s where the similaritie
 s end. \n \nIn Floyd you roll along through the soul of Appalachia farm la
 nd\, with punchy climbs and amazing descents. In Craig… let’s just say
  things get a little bigger\, a little bolder\, and we can’t wait to sha
 re it with you. \n \nOpposing the “Dragons Back” our current Mountaine
 er courses traverse the beautiful exposure of Bald Knob before dropping ba
 ck down to the valley and crossing the river by foot bridge and then fast 
 rolling home.  https://www.craigcountyva.gov/calendar.aspx?EID=729
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261107
DTSTAMP;TZID=America/New_York:20260323T103339
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261107
LAST-MODIFIED;TZID=America/New_York:20260323T103339
LOCATION: -   New Castle VA 24127
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Appalachian Mountaineer 
UID:729
URL:/common/modules/iCalendar/iCalendar.aspx?feed=calendar&catID=14
END:VEVENT
